Translation patch: `escaped` (SQL string quoting, used by `Value::as_sql`)

Change: The loops `for c in input.chars() { .. output.push(c) .. }` over a `String` output become index loops over the bytes `trusted::str_as_bytes(input)` pushing bytes into a `Vec<u8>` (`'\''` becomes `b'\''`, etc.), and the result is `trusted::string_from_utf8(output)` (patch 40), with `Err(_) => unreachable!()`. `String::with_capacity(input.len())` becomes `Vec::with_capacity(input.len())`.
Why: Aeneas does not model `Chars::next` (opaque in its library) or `String::push`.
Behaviour: Identical output. In UTF-8 a `char` below U+0080 is encoded as the single byte of the same value, and every byte of the encoding of any other `char` is >= 0x80. Every character the function compares against (`'\''`, `'\x00'`, `'\n'`, `'\r'`, `'\\'`, `'"'`, `'\x1a'`) and every character it inserts is ASCII, so a byte equals one of them exactly when it is that whole character; all other bytes (including all bytes of non-ASCII characters) are copied unchanged, in order. The output bytes are therefore exactly the UTF-8 encoding of the original output `String`; in particular they are valid UTF-8, so `string_from_utf8` returns `Ok` and the `unreachable!()` branch is never taken.

